# SRG-APP-000096-AU-000690  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must produce audit records containing information
# to establish when (date and time) the events occurred.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000096-AU-000690
group:           V-221909
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000131
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    Splunk assigns _time to every indexed record, and DATETIME_CONFIG selects
                 whether that time is extracted from the record's own text or replaced by
                 the server's processing time.

governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.

check:           props.conf [] DATETIME_CONFIG not_in NONE|CURRENT

external:        The accuracy of the recorded time rests on host clock synchronization,
                 performed by the operating system's time service and assessed under
                 SRG-APP-000086-AU-000030.

citation:        DIRECTION. Removed props.conf MAX_TIMESTAMP_LOOKAHEAD min 1.
                 props.conf.spec states "If set to 0 or -1, the length constraint for
                 timestamp recognition is effectively disabled" - 0 and -1 remove the
                 character limit so the extractor scans the whole event, which recognizes
                 timestamps at least as well as the default of 128, not worse. The
                 condition reads those values as if they switched timestamping off, so it
                 fails exactly the configurations it should pass. The setting bounds a
                 search window for performance and appears in neither the check nor the fix
                 text.
finding:         Timestamp extraction is disabled for the sourcetypes in scope
                 (DATETIME_CONFIG set to NONE or CURRENT), so the time on a stored record
                 is when Splunk processed it rather than when the event occurred.
